Web source: web/src/features/vehicles/components/VehicleHeader.tsx — a presentational header fed { vehicle,
state, onRefetchState } props. Data sources mapped to shared P1/S8 state holders: useVehicles (+ the page's
useVehicleState) and useWakeVehicle; useTranslation -> P1/S10 ILocalizer facade. No HTTP in the view.

Parity reproduced:
  - Layout: back affordance (web <Link to="/vehicles">, raised as NavigationRequested("/vehicles")) + title
    (display_name || vin || t('common.vehicle','Vehicle')) beside the live StatusBadge (TsStatusBadge with the
    web badge-dot palette mapped to themed tokens) + model/trim/VIN subtitle + the Wake Up button (web
    useWakeVehicle: TsButton, IsLoading while in flight, on success refetches state after a settle window —
    the web setTimeout(onRefetchState, 5000)).
  - Status derivation: native VehicleHeaderStatus.Derive mirrors web getVehicleStatus/deriveVehicleStatus
    exactly (is_charging > speed>0 > recognised FSM state > online; no vehicle or no live state => offline).
  - States (every state renders; never a blank box): loading (skeleton bar), loaded, empty (friendly header
    with the common.vehicle fallback title + offline badge + disabled wake + a hint), error (QueryError +
    retry), stale (stale chip + freshness auto-refresh), offline (offline chip + cached header). Wake result
    is surfaced inline (toast-equivalent) and announced.
  - i18n (every string keyed; no hardcoded English): the two source keys common.vehicle + common.wakeUp; the
    wake toasts toast.vehicles.wake.success / .error; common.back/refresh/retry/loading/stale/offline;
    vehicles.detail.title (surface name), vehicles.emptyTitle, vehicles.loadError, vehicle.state.{token}. All
    resolve through the ILocalizer facade (KeyEcho + Passthrough asserted in tests).
  - Accessibility: surface AutomationPeer is a Header named by the projected "<name>, <status>"; back, wake and
    refresh each expose a Narrator name; the wake result is a live region; no custom motion beyond the shared
    FadeIn (reduced-motion honoured by TsFadeIn/TsSkeleton).
  - Telemetry: view.opened slug=VehicleHeader on first load; vehicle.wake.requested / vehicle.wake.resolved
    (success=true|false) on the mutation — PII-safe (never a VIN / name / vehicle id) per the P1/S11 contract.

Deliverable gate (build + headless unit tests + format + placeholders) = all 0. The full-solution dotnet test
